module example.com/scratch

go 1.27
-- .kiln/specs/x.md --
# Spec 1: x

Status: Approved, 2026-11-12

## Overview

## Goals

## Non-goals

## Open Questions

## Acceptance tests

### 1. X answers

- **Given**: nothing.
- **When**: X is called.
- **Then**: it answers 42.

## Technical Plan

`scratch.X()` answers an int.

## Alternatives Considered
-- _given/code/x.go --
// Package scratch is where kiln's builds land.
package scratch

// X answers 42.
func X() int { return 42 }
-- _given/code/harness/h.go --
// Package harness is what the acceptance tests run through.
package harness

// Ready is true.
const Ready = true
-- _given/tests/acceptance/x/x_test.go --
package x_test

import (
	"testing"

	"example.com/scratch"
)

func TestAT1(t *testing.T) {
	if got := scratch.X(); got != 42 {
		t.Fatalf("X answers %d, want 42", got)
	}
}
